                            <note>This manuscript was commissioned by King Dawit’s daughter (whose name is spelled a variety of ways in different manuscripts, including as Dǝl Mängǝśa, Dal Mägäsa, Dal Mängäsa; her baptismal name is Batra ’Āron). She donated the manuscript to the church she built, Betä Ləḥem church in the town of Gayänt, near the city of Däbrä Tabor in Ethiopia</note>
                        </origin>
